{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What advantage then hath the Jew? or what is the profit of circumcision?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Much every way: first of all, that they were intrusted with the oracles of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what if some were without faith? shall their want of faith make of none effect the faithfulness of God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God forbid: yea, let God be found true, but every man a liar; as it is written,That thou mightest be justified in thy words,\nAnd mightest prevail when thou comest into judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if our unrighteousness commendeth the righteousness of God, what shall we say? Is God unrighteous who visiteth with wrath? (I speak after the manner of men.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God forbid: for then how shall God judge the world?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if the truth of God through my lie abounded unto his glory, why am I also still judged as a sinner?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and why not (as we are slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say), Let us do evil, that good may come? whose condemnation is just.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What then? are we better than they? No, in no wise: for we before laid to the charge both of Jews and Greeks, that they are all under sin;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "as it is written,There is none righteous, no, not one;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is none that understandeth,\nThere is none that seeketh after God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have all turned aside, they are together become unprofitable;\nThere is none that doeth good, no, not so much as one:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their throat is an open sepulchre;\nWith their tongues they have used deceit:The poison of asps is under their lips:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their feet are swift to shed blood;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Destruction and misery are in their ways;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the way of peace have they not known:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is no fear of God before their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it speaketh to them that are under the law; that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may be brought under the judgment of God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "because by the works of the law shall no flesh be justified in his sight; for through the law ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the knowledge of sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now apart from the law a righteousness of God hath been manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "even the righteousness of God through faith in Jesus Christ unto all them that believe; for there is no distinction;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for all have sinned, and fall short of the glory of God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "whom God set forth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a propitiation, through faith, in his blood, to show his righteousness because of the passing over of the sins done aforetime, in the forbearance of God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for the showing, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", of his righteousness at this present season: that he might himself be just, and the justifier of him that hath faith in Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where then is the glorying? It is excluded. By what manner of law? of works? Nay: but by a law of faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We reckon therefore that a man is justified by faith apart from the works of the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or is God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Jews only? is he not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Gentiles also? Yea, of Gentiles also:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "if so be that God is one, and he shall justify the circumcision by faith, and the uncircumcision through faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.3.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:ROM.3.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do we then make the law of none effect through faith? God forbid: nay, we establish the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
